# Append-only ledgers: two processes appending in the same minute must both
# survive a rebase. Union keeps every line from both sides. Each line carries
# its own timestamp and run id, so order across writers does not matter.
#
# For a week the loser of that rebase lost its lines, and real fills vanished
# from the record while the broker quietly held the positions.
ledger.jsonl        merge=union
ledger_fast.jsonl   merge=union
ledger_movers.jsonl merge=union

# NOT the research chain. Interleaving two writers' rows breaks the hash
# chain by construction; a conflict there must fail loudly, and the class fix
# is a single writer. Union would hide exactly the defect it exists to catch.
research_log.jsonl  -merge
